<section vertical-align="center">
  <grid spacing="none">
    <grid-item>
      <p role="eyebrow">Illustrated object reconstructions</p>
      <h2>Everyday objects carry big questions</h2>
      <grid recipe="images-text" image-aspect="landscape" image-shape="rounded" spacing="small">
        <grid-item colspan="15">
          <ai-image image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" aspect-ratio="landscape" prompt="Layered cut-paper museum illustration of a nineteenth-century tax paper on warm cream paper beside a few plain coins and a red seal, colored-pencil shading, postcard red and sun yellow accents, no people, no legible text, no logos"/>
          <h4>Tax paper</h4>
          <p>Who pays—and who decides the rules?</p>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item colspan="15">
          <ai-image image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" aspect-ratio="landscape" prompt="Layered cut-paper museum illustration of a folded schematic map on warm cream paper, river-blue route lines and one postcard-red region marker, visibly folded paper edges, no exact borders, no labels, no legible text"/>
          <h4>Map</h4>
          <p>Who should govern the region?</p>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item colspan="15">
          <ai-image image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" aspect-ratio="landscape" prompt="Layered cut-paper museum illustration of a tied letter from home opened beside a travel bag on warm cream paper, soft colored-pencil shading, river-blue ribbon and postcard-red wax seal, no readable writing, no people"/>
          <h4>Letter</h4>
          <p>How do people learn what is happening?</p>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item colspan="15">
          <ai-image image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" aspect-ratio="landscape" prompt="Layered cut-paper museum illustration of a practical food basket holding bread, dried beans and simple produce on warm cream paper, colored-pencil shading with sun-yellow and river-blue cloth accents, ordinary household scale, no text, no people"/>
          <h4>Food basket</h4>
          <p>How do families keep daily life going?</p>
        </grid-item>
      </grid>
      <p><b>Objects help us study political ideas and ordinary experiences together.</b></p>
    </grid-item>
  </grid>
</section>